<title>USA: USDA extends GSM-102 credit to Pakistan for FY97.</title>
<headline>USDA extends GSM-102 credit to Pakistan for FY97.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Agriculture Department has authorized $250 million in credit guarantees for sales of U.S. agricultural commodities to Pakistan under the Commodity Credit Corporation's Export Credit Gurantee Program for fiscal year 1997.</p>
<p>Commodities eligible to be purchased under the program include breeder livestock, cotton, feed grains, oilseeds, pulses, vegetable oils, wheat and wheat flour and wood pulp and wood chips.</p>
</text>
